/* Language packs. One entry per language code; English is not in here — it is
   written out at the point it is used in assets/js/app.js, as the second
   argument to t(), so the source still reads as English prose and a key missing
   from a pack renders in English rather than as a key.

   The game's own nomenclature is deliberately not translated in any pack. An
   item stays a Plump helmet, a building a Metalsmith's Forge, a job on its menu
   Brew Drink, and a picker's options — the metals, the qualities, the drink
   kinds, the materials — stay the words the game puts on the screen you are
   alt-tabbing away from. A translated menu entry would be a worse answer than
   an untranslated one. What a pack carries is everything this site says *about*
   them: headings, labels, legends and every note.

   `ui` is keyed by a short string and holds the text written into the views.
   {n}-style holes rather than concatenation, because Spanish does not put the
   number, the noun and the preposition in the order English does.

   `data` is keyed by the id a data file already carries, and holds the prose
   that lives beside the facts. Table *rows* are never in here — those are the
   game's words — and `tableCols` only replaces a header row that still matches
   the original column for column. */

